# One completed lap of Talon's Junction White, Time Trial, Venom, Assegai.
#
# Recorded by `scripts/psp-autopilot.py` steering the original along the disc's
# own spline (`oag-trace track`), one closed-loop decision per tick at a
# `Ship_UpdateCraft` breakpoint. Every line below is exactly what the emulator
# was sent, shifted two ticks later so the file reads in `oag-trace`'s
# convention rather than the breakpoint's - so replay it into the emulator with
# `psp-trace.py --script-lead 2` and into our own physics with
# `oag-trace run --script ... --script-lead 2`. See docs/tools/oag-trace.md.
#
# **The lead is needed on BOTH sides and the sentence above once said otherwise.**
# Sending tick k+2 at tick k means the first two lines' opening ticks are never
# sent at all, so a capture is this file with its first two ticks released, and
# a replay that applies them drives an input the original never saw. Two ticks
# survive the whole run because the steering ramp never settles on its target:
# unshifted, this file's replay ends 8 degrees off heading by tick 70, meets a
# wall at tick 147 that the original never touches, and travels 754 units where
# the original travelled 1,045. That was recorded as M4's blocker for a session.
#
# The run this came off finished the lap: the game's own HUD read `Lap 2 of 3`
# with `best 1.11.08` at tick 3087, which is the game timing the lap rather than
# this file's author claiming one. 3,146 ticks, 5,169 units travelled, peak
# 164 units/s.
#
# Read this before assuming what it is: it is a faithful record of the inputs of
# a lap that happened, and it is NOT a reproducible emulator lap. Sent back into
# PPSSPP from a fresh restart it travels 860 units and stops against a wall,
# because `psp-drive.py restart` repeats the craft's start position exactly and
# its heading only to about 2.5 degrees. On our own side it is fully
# deterministic. The measurement is in docs/tools/oag-trace.md.

